        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8bfc5807-981d-5caf-b050-c872ea154465",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anatole Litvak, Kinji Fukasaku, Olivia de Havilland\n- Films: The Snake Pit, The Adventures of Robin Hood, Gone with the Wind, To Each His Own, The Heiress\n- Roles: filmmaker, director, producer, screenwriter, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Anatole Litvak was born on May 21, 1902, and he was a Russian-born American filmmaker who wrote, directed, and produced films in various countries and languages.\n- Kinji Fukasaku was born on July 3, 1930, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- The Adventures of Robin Hood was released in 1938, and Olivia de Havilland was best known for her early screen performance in it.\n- Gone with the Wind was released in 1939, and Olivia de Havilland was best known for her early screen performance in it.\n- To Each His Own was released in 1946, and Olivia de Havilland was best known for her later award-winning performance in it.\n- The Snake Pit is a 1948 American drama film directed by Anatole Litvak and starring Olivia de Havilland, Mark Stevens, Leo Genn, Celeste Holm, Beulah Bondi, and Lee Patrick.\n- Olivia de Havilland was best known for her later award-winning performances in The Snake Pit (1948) and The Heiress (1949).\n- Anatole Litvak died on December 15, 1974.\n- Kinji Fukasaku died on January 12, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
